' @fileoverview When a spoken query reaches the search screen's voice box, decide whether to
' submit it now, hold it, or ignore it.
'
' Extracted from SearchScreen so the rule is unit-tested with plain values, the same reason
' searchRoute.bs holds the route-context rule. The firmware writes one spoken query to the
' box more than once while the viewer is still dictating (measured 2026-10-18 on a Streaming
' Stick 4K: two writes per word), and each write used to be a submit. So a write during
' dictation is held, and the held text is submitted once, when dictation ends.
'
' Each function takes the text held so far and returns the next step:
' { pending: the text to hold now, submit: the text to submit now, or "" }.

namespace searchVoice

  ' The box's text changed.
  '
  ' @param pending     - the text held so far ("" if none)
  ' @param text        - the box's new text; "" is the screen clearing it after a submit
  ' @param isDictating - whether the viewer is still speaking
  function onText(pending as string, text as string, isDictating as boolean) as object
    if text = "" then return { pending: pending, submit: "" }
    if isDictating then return { pending: text, submit: "" }
    return { pending: "", submit: text }
  end function

  ' Dictation started or ended. Ending submits what was held, once.
  '
  ' @param pending     - the text held so far ("" if none)
  ' @param isDictating - whether the viewer is still speaking
  function onDictatingChanged(pending as string, isDictating as boolean) as object
    if isDictating or pending = "" then return { pending: pending, submit: "" }
    return { pending: "", submit: pending }
  end function

end namespace
